    "body": "The first joint native update loses all8 accepted entry successes while its served continuation field remainszero. This adds an explicit diagnostic mode to identify whether Source (Context/Potential), Generate coefficients or their combination is sufficient for that first-update loss.\n\nThe mode authenticates the retained parent and joint1 checkpoints, reuses exact Generate donor bytes, and independently reloads a source/Generate-bound zero-v2 field for each of four combinations. Both original combinations must reproduce saved512-row entry evidence; the joint initial checkpoint must match the independently admitted accepted parent. With Source fixed, swapping Generate must preserve bank replay, selection, factual state, physical Copy aliases and raw Copy scores. All4096 Generate actions remain present, with labels used only after four native forwards.\n\nThe report keeps all512 row identities, exact normalized probability/margin contrasts and original8 outcome sets separate from the remaining504 rows. Mixed combinations are derived unaccepted diagnostic artifacts. Normal consumer admission and default own-prefix behavior remain intact.\n\nExecuted source `378a89581216ecd5bcb0217f3b5a9e74bcee87e8` passes formatting,16 focused tests and release compilation. Mathematical/adversarial source review finds no blocker. Actual2048-call native execution, both512-row diagonal parity checks, Rust seal verification and independent compact saved-evidence audit pass.\n\nCorrect entry counts in S0G0,S0G1,S1G0,S1G1 order are **8/8/0/0**. All original8 losses are Source-alone sufficient; the other504 remain wrong in every arm. Two original rows retain exact selected-candidate identity despite losing entry, so selection change is not necessary for every loss. No mixed model is promoted.\n\nA further saved-only reader reconstructs the exact first119-position training objective:7.2967103431→7.0420308865. The initial value matches the actual forward receipt; independent arithmetic review confirms the phase-balanced weights. Thus aggregate drawn-batch loss improves while outside-batch successes collapse. The next proposed repair is supervised reference replay from all parent-correct teacher positions across512/all phases, keeping Context learning active; this is NOT_RUN and requires a prospective weighting/schedule/resource card.\n\nNative execution31.576s/591292KiB RSS;2048 forwards20.880s, independent reader4.402s. The report is10.39MB within128MiB; no GPU or local build. Evidence, source reconstruction, executable, config, checks and reviews are preserved at privateHF revision `703b315a520f5cfeb5fc9071c53571389d4380bd`, prefix `codex/astra-component-entry/entry-378a895812`; archive SHA256 `74a9baf9f3c59017c033d769292aaf538651d1f588890bf0fcb620596ac3b111`, freshly downloaded and verified. Final documentation head is `ff4b75ca60373d63b6fd80c2eb5e0232c6afdcc9`, with identical executed Rust; exact final formatting,16 tests, release build and claims pass; independent final-head review finds no blocker. Final checks, reviews and saved-batch evidence are separately preserved at private HF `9a9117153032abb801799c258dec65b597d618e5`, prefix `codex/astra-component-entry/final-delivery-ff4b75ca60`, with all17 files freshly downloaded and verified. No fit, complete-reply, transfer, chat, final64 attribution or geometry advantage is claimed. No dose/rate/seed sweep is introduced.\n\nReferences #820\n",
